|> Exercise
    handle=_construct_dimensionless_output_

    |> CodexSuggestion
        Given a differentiable function $f : [\s] \ra [\s]$,
        can you construct a function of signature $[\s] \ra [1]$?

    |> Solution
        |> CodexSuggestion
            The derivative $f'$ has the required signature.

            Alternatively, $f/f$ has this signature wherever $f$ is nonzero.
